# OxiBonsai — model artifact checksums (sec-12 / RAG-EVAL-IMG-32 / deps-08).
#
# Verify with (from the repository root, after downloading into `models/`):
#   shasum -a 256 -c scripts/checksums.sha256 --ignore-missing
# or, where GNU coreutils is available:
#   sha256sum -c scripts/checksums.sha256 --ignore-missing
#
# `--ignore-missing` is required because most developers only ever download
# a subset of these (a 27B PTQ1_0/PQ2_0 GGUF is 6-7 GB each) — this file is
# a manifest of everything the project can produce/fetch, not a checklist
# every checkout must have on disk.
#
# `scripts/download_ternary.sh` and `scripts/download_tokenizer.sh` run this
# verification automatically after every download and fail loudly on a
# mismatch; this file is what they check against.
#
# ── AUTHORITATIVE vs ADVISORY ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two different kinds of entry live in this file, and they carry different
# guarantees:
#
#   AUTHORITATIVE — the file is meant to be a byte-for-byte published
#   artifact, fetched directly from its HuggingFace repo with no local
#   processing. A mismatch here means corruption, a tampered mirror, or an
#   upstream revision bump, and downloader scripts treat it as a hard
#   failure.
#
#   PROVENANCE for the Bonsai 2 27B entries specifically (sec-12) — two
#   separate sources, cited separately because they carry different
#   authority; do not merge them into one unsourced claim:
#     - CONFIRMED BY THE PROJECT OWNER: the repo is
#       `prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf`, holding
#       Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PTQ1_0.gguf (5946648928 B),
#       Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0.gguf (7206168928 B) and
#       Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-mmproj-Q8_0.gguf (629246976 B) —
#       independently corroborated by the file list in the README of
#       PrismML's Bonsai-demo repository. This is `OXI_BONSAI2_REPO`'s
#       default in scripts/download_ternary.sh.
#     - FROM `MODEL-FORMATS.md` in PrismML's Bonsai-demo repository (its
#       table of model files): the third language GGUF,
#       Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-Q2_0-prism-fork-required.gguf, is deliberately
#       kept OUT of that repo (mainline llama.cpp already
#       knows ggml type id 42 and would silently misdecode this file's
#       group-128 layout as the official group-64 Q2_0) and is published
#       separately, for testing only, in
#       `prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf-dev` — this is
#       `OXI_BONSAI2_DEV_REPO`'s default.
#   The three recorded hashes below were computed with `shasum -a 256`
#   against the real files in the maintainers' own development checkout
#   (`models/`) on 2026-09-21 (53107f53...3ee3 PTQ1_0, 3907dc16...2ec1
#   PQ2_0, 6807ede6...1903 mmproj) — treat them as authoritative for the
#   two confirmed repos above. docs/models.md lists which model files have a
#   verified hash and which do not.
#
#   ADVISORY — the file is produced by *local* conversion
#   (`oxibonsai convert`, run by `download_ternary.sh` against upstream
#   unpacked safetensors). Its exact bytes depend on the converter's own
#   version/behavior, not just the upstream source, so a hash drift here
#   can be an intentional converter improvement rather than corruption.
#   These entries are still verified (a good regression signal: "did last
#   night's converter change silently alter output for the same input on
#   the same machine?"), but a mismatch is reported as a WARNING that
#   names this trade-off, not a hard failure that blocks the download.
#
# Regenerate an entry after an intentional change with:
#   shasum -a 256 models/<file> | awk '{print $1 "  models/" $2}'
# (adjust the printed path to strip the shasum-emitted directory prefix).
#
# Recorded 2026-09-21 against the files present in this project's own
# development checkout (COOLJAPAN OU / Team KitaSan, Apple M3).
#
# The Bonsai 2 27B family is exactly THREE language GGUFs (PTQ1_0, PQ2_0,
# and the legacy-layout Q2_0 requiring PrismML's `prism` llama.cpp fork —
# see docs/models.md, "ggml type id 42: three layouts under one id", on why
# ggml type id 42 is ambiguous between mainline group-64 and this group-128
# PrismML layout) plus the mmproj vision projector — four artifacts total.
# Only the first two language GGUFs' full bytes have been hashed; the third
# (Q2_0-prism-fork-required) has a MISSING placeholder below instead of a
# hash — see that entry's comment for why and how to fill it in.
#
# Coverage note (deps-08): this file also lists the three
# previous-generation (non-Bonsai-2) 27B GGUFs as MISSING placeholders
# (Bonsai-27B-Q1_0, Ternary-Bonsai-27B-PQ2_0, Ternary-Bonsai-27B-Q2_0) —
# see the dedicated section below. Every Bonsai 27B GGUF the project loads
# therefore has either a verified hash or an explicit MISSING placeholder
# here. This is NOT a claim that every model file the tables of PrismML's
# Bonsai-demo `MODEL-FORMATS.md` name is covered — e.g. the official group-64
# `*_g64`/`*-PQ2_0` files for the 1.7B/4B/8B/27B sizes are outside this
# manifest's scope; do not infer their absence means anything.
#
# (Note: separator lines below are a lone "#", not blank — a truly blank
# line makes both `shasum -c` and `sha256sum -c` print a spurious "N lines
# are improperly formatted" warning even though verification still
# succeeds; a comment line does not.)
#
# ── AUTHORITATIVE: published GGUF, downloaded verbatim ───────────────────
# fetched by: curl (see scripts/cli.sh / README "Quick Start") — no
# dedicated download script owns this one.
