# PrismML's legacy group-128 layout, NOT mainline llama.cpp's official
# group-64 Q2_0 -- reading it with a stock llama.cpp would silently
# misdecode the blocks, hence the filename warning; it needs PrismML's
# `prism` fork, see docs/models.md). Per `MODEL-FORMATS.md` in PrismML's
# Bonsai-demo repository, it is fetched from
# `prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf-dev` (testing only), NOT the main
# repo above. Only this file's first 64 MB (its GGUF header) has been
# inspected -- the full multi-gigabyte payload has not been fetched, so no
# byte-exact sha256 could be computed. `scripts/download_ternary.sh 27b-q2_0` (and
# `27b-all`) will fetch it; `verify_checksum`'s "no checksum recorded yet"
# branch fires harmlessly until this placeholder is replaced with a real
# hash line via:
#   shasum -a 256 models/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-Q2_0-prism-fork-required.gguf | awk '{print $1 "  " $2}'
#
# ── AUTHORITATIVE, MISSING: previous-generation (non-Bonsai-2) 27B family ─
